Brazil's white shirts with blue collars that were worn in the final game were, in the wake of the defeat, subject to criticism by the country's sports federation for being "unpatriotic", with pressure mounting to change the colours.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/world-cup-2014-meet-the-uruguay-fan-who-designed-brazils-iconic-yellow-kit-9569511.html |title=World Cup 2014: Meet the Uruguay fan who designed Brazil's iconic yellow kit |last=Bellos |first=Alex |date=27 June 2014 |website=The Independent |access-date=8 July 2018 |archive-date=8 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180708220624/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/world-cup-2014-meet-the-uruguay-fan-who-designed-brazils-iconic-yellow-kit-9569511.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In 1953 and with the support of the [[Brazilian Sports Confederation]],<ref name="NewYorker">{{cite magazine |last=Michaud |first=Jon |url=https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-writer-who-designed-brazils-soccer-uniform |title=The Writer Who Designed Brazil's Soccer Uniform |date=2 June 2014 |magazine=The New Yorker |access-date=27 November 2022 |archive-date=28 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221128000931/https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-writer-who-designed-brazils-soccer-uniform |url-status=live }}</ref> a competition was held by the newspaper ''[[Correio da Manhã (Brazil)|Correio da Manhã]]'' to design a new outfit,<ref name="AldyrGarciaSchlee">{{cite news |last=Garcia Schlee |first=Aldyr |authorlink=Aldyr Schlee |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2009/mar/14/brazil-wear-yellow-first-time |title=14 March 1954: Brazil play in yellow for the first time |date=14 March 2009 |access-date=27 November 2022 |work=The Guardian}}</ref> with the rule being that it must incorporate the colours of the [[Flag of Brazil|national flag]]. Eventually, the competition was won by newspaper illustrator [[Aldyr Garcia Schlee]],<ref name="GoldenYears">{{cite web |last=Bellos |first=Alex |url=https://www.theguardian.com/observer/osm/story/0,,1123140,00.html |title=The golden years |date=18 January 2004 |work=The Guardian |access-date=27 November 2022}}</ref> who came up with the design of a yellow shirt with a green trim, blue shorts with white trim, and white socks.<ref name="AldyrGarciaSchlee"/> Schlee had initially been deterred from using all four colours, believing that yellow and white was too similar to the [[Holy See]].<ref name="NewYorker"/>

The new kit was first used in March 1954 against [[Chile national football team|Chile]], and has been used ever since.<ref>{{cite news |last=Smith |first=Ben |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/magazine-27809268 |title=The story of Brazil's 'sacred' yellow and green jersey |date=28 June 2014 |access-date=28 June 2014 |work=BBC News |archive-date=28 June 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140628030042/http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/magazine-27809268 |url-status=live }}</ref> The runner-up design was a green shirt, white shorts, and yellow socks.<ref name="GoldenYears"/> When Brazil first won the World Cup in 1958, they wore an improvised blue kit as the new colours clashed with those of hosts Sweden.<ref name="NewYorker"/>

==="Phantom of '50"===
The term "Phantom of '50" was later used to refer to the fear that Brazilians and [[Brazil national football team]] feel of the [[Uruguay national football team]] due to this loss. Each time Brazil and Uruguay play at Maracanã Stadium, the theme resurfaces.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://oglobo.globo.com/esportes/copa-2014/apos-classificacao-do-uruguai-fantasma-de-50-ja-esta-no-brasil-10838153|title=Após classificação do Uruguai, 'fantasma de 50' já está no Brasil|date=21 November 2013|website=O Globo|access-date=4 December 2022|archive-date=4 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221204182904/https://oglobo.globo.com/esportes/copa-2014/apos-classificacao-do-uruguai-fantasma-de-50-ja-esta-no-brasil-10838153|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.dn.pt/desporto/futebol-internacional/o-fantasma-de-50-ja-esta-no-brasil-3544473.html|title=O fantasma de 50 já está no Brasil|website=www.dn.pt|access-date=4 December 2022|archive-date=4 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221204182904/https://www.dn.pt/desporto/futebol-internacional/o-fantasma-de-50-ja-esta-no-brasil-3544473.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.terra.com.br/esportes/futebol/copa-2014/capitao-lugano-critica-fantasma-de-50-e-cita-ligacoes-do-brasil,e6293367ccf72410VgnVCM10000098cceb0aRCRD.html|title=Capitão, Lugano critica "Fantasma de 50" e cita ligações do Brasil|website=Terra|access-date=4 December 2022|archive-date=4 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221204182905/https://www.terra.com.br/esportes/futebol/copa-2014/capitao-lugano-critica-fantasma-de-50-e-cita-ligacoes-do-brasil,e6293367ccf72410VgnVCM10000098cceb0aRCRD.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 1993, after losing points in important matches (two draws with [[Ecuador national football team|Ecuador]] and Uruguay themselves, and a loss to [[Bolivia national football team|Bolivia]] in first round of the qualifiers), Brazil was struggling to [[1994 FIFA World Cup qualification (CONMEBOL)|qualify]] for the [[1994 FIFA World Cup]]. The final match of the qualifying South American group between Brazil and Uruguay was tense, surrounded by fear, as Brazil needed to win the game to qualify. Brazil beat and eliminated Uruguay by 2–0, with two goals by [[Romário]] at the end of the second half, who had been ignored in the tournament and was urgently called in to save Brazil, who would go on to win the tournament.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://infograficos.estadao.com.br/jogo_da_minha_vida/romario|title=Romário: O jogo da minha vida. Brasil 2 x 0 Uruguai. Eliminatória da Copa – 1993 – Especiais – Estadao.com.br|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203121001/http://infograficos.estadao.com.br/jogo_da_minha_vida/romario|archive-date=3 December 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref>

The theme reappeared in the Brazilian press as Uruguay qualified for the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] hosted by Brazil.<ref>[http://www.gazetaesportiva.net/noticia/2013/11/copa-2014-brasil/felipao-ri-de-fantasma-de-50-e-usa-grupo-jovem-contra-assombracao.html Felipão ri de “fantasma de 50” e usa grupo jovem contra assombração | Gazeta Esportiva.Net] {{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131202042441/http://www.gazetaesportiva.net/noticia/2013/11/copa-2014-brasil/felipao-ri-de-fantasma-de-50-e-usa-grupo-jovem-contra-assombracao.html |date=2 December 2013 }}</ref> Uruguay often emphasized the theme, giving the team motivation and encouragement in matches against Brazil.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.terra.com.br/esportes/futebol/copa-2014/fantasma-do-maracanazo-provoca-brasileiros-e-posta-foto-de-bumbuns,1d8546b2f4b72410VgnVCM5000009ccceb0aRCRD.html|title="Fantasma do Maracanazo" provoca brasileiros e posta foto de bumbuns|website=Terra|access-date=4 December 2022|archive-date=4 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221204182902/https://www.terra.com.br/esportes/futebol/copa-2014/fantasma-do-maracanazo-provoca-brasileiros-e-posta-foto-de-bumbuns,1d8546b2f4b72410VgnVCM5000009ccceb0aRCRD.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Ironically, however, Uruguay lost 2–0 and were eliminated by [[Colombia national football team|Colombia]] at the very same Maracanã Stadium in the [[2014 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Colombia vs Uruguay|round of 16 of the tournament]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/29/colombia-uruguay-james-rodriguez|title=Colombia's James Rodríguez seeks top honours and sends warning to Brazil|date=29 June 2014 |work=Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref> Brazil's path again had a hard defeat, this time a 1–7 humiliation in the semi-final with [[Germany national football team|Germany]] in [[Belo Horizonte]], the game was subsequently known as "[[Mineirazo]]", given it took place at the [[Mineirão]] stadium and echoed the same sense of defeat as in 1950.<ref name="FIFANumbers">{{cite web |title=The Mineirazo in numbers |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=7/news=the-mineirazo-in-numbers-2402146.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140709023442/http://www.fifa.com//worldcup/news/y=2014/m=7/news=the-mineirazo-in-numbers-2402146.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=9 July 2014 |date=8 July 2014 |access-date=8 July 2014 |work=[[FIFA]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |language=es |url=http://www.pagina12.com.ar/diario/ultimas/20-250319-2014-07-08.html |title=Del Maracanazo al Mineirazo |trans-title=From Maracanazo to Mineirazo |newspaper=Página 12 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140713202930/http://www.pagina12.com.ar/diario/ultimas/20-250319-2014-07-08.html |archive-date=13 July 2014 |url-status=live }}</ref> Tereza Borba, adoptive daughter of goalkeeper [[Moacir Barbosa]], who was scapegoated for the defeat for years, said the 2014 loss was enough to redeem her father's legacy, and most of the Brazilian media took the opportunity to contrast the 2014 semi-final as an embarrassment compared to the close defeat in the Maracanazo.<ref name=globe>{{cite web |url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/sports/soccer/world-cup/brazil-losers-on-the-field-now-turn-to-the-blame-game/article19524752/ |title=Brazil, losers on the field, now turn to the blame game |last=Nolen |first=Stephanie |work=The Globe and Mail |date=9 July 2014 |access-date=1 September 2014 |archive-date=15 July 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150715055820/http://www.theglobeandmail.com/sports/soccer/world-cup/brazil-losers-on-the-field-now-turn-to-the-blame-game/article19524752/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://esportes.r7.com/futebol/copa-do-mundo-2014/jogadores-de-50-enfim-sao-perdoados-apos-mineirazo-09072014 |title=Jogadores de 50 enfim são perdoados após Mineirazo |publisher=R7 ([[Rede Record]]) |date=9 July 2014 |access-date= 5 September 2014 |language=pt |last=Avelar |first=André |work=R7.com |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140710144647/http://esportes.r7.com/futebol/copa-do-mundo-2014/jogadores-de-50-enfim-sao-perdoados-apos-mineirazo-09072014 |archive-date=10 July 2014 |url-status=live }}</ref> Ghiggia himself, the only player from either 1950 squad who lived to see the 2014 loss, stated that while both games were traumatic, they could not be compared as the 1950 game had more at stake.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.efe.com/efe/noticias/brasil/esportes/maracanazo-diferente-porque-foi-uma-final-afirma-ghiggia/3/18/2365675 |title="O Maracanazo é diferente porque foi uma final", afirma Ghiggia |publisher=Agência EFE |date=9 July 2014 |access-date=1 September 2014 |language=pt |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140903085428/http://www.efe.com/efe/noticias/brasil/esportes/maracanazo-diferente-porque-foi-uma-final-afirma-ghiggia/3/18/2365675 |archive-date=3 September 2014 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Ghiggia was the last surviving player from the game; he died on 16 July 2015, exactly 65 years after scoring the decisive goal, at the age of 88.<ref>{{cite web |title=Carrasco em 1950, Ghiggia morre no aniversário do Maracanazo |url=http://esportes.terra.com.br/futebol/ghiggia-morre-aos-88-anos-no-aniversario-do-maracanazo,369a73e90f7d334252b262f468cfd0013x0hRCRD.html |publisher=Terra |date=16 July 2015 |access-date=17 July 2015 |language=pt |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150717225841/http://esportes.terra.com.br/futebol/ghiggia-morre-aos-88-anos-no-aniversario-do-maracanazo,369a73e90f7d334252b262f468cfd0013x0hRCRD.html |archive-date=17 July 2015 |url-status=live }}</ref> Schlee died on 17 November 2018, aged 83.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-latin-america-46243922 |title=Aldyr Schlee, designer of Brazil's famous yellow jersey, dies |date=17 November 2018 |work=BBC News |access-date=27 November 2022 |archive-date=28 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221128000931/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-latin-america-46243922 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Garcia |first=Sandra |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/18/obituaries/aldyr-garcia-schlee-dead.html |title=Aldyr Schlee, 83, Dies; Created Brazil Soccer Team's Iconic Jersey |date=18 November 2018 |work=The New York Times |access-date=27 November 2022 |archive-date=28 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221128000952/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/18/obituaries/aldyr-garcia-schlee-dead.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

